def max_dot_product(nums1, nums2):
    n, m = len(nums1), len(nums2)
    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]

    for i in range(1, n + 1):
        for j in range(1, m + 1):
            dp[i][j] = max(
                dp[i-1][j],
                dp[i][j-1],
                nums1[i-1] * nums2[j-1] + max(0, dp[i-1][j-1])
            )

    return dp[n][m]
```
</code>

This solution has a time complexity of O(n*m) and a space complexity of O(n*m), where n and m are the lengths of `nums1` and `nums2`, respectively....
