To calculate dp[i][j], we’ll consider each cut k in the range i+1 to j-1 and calculate the cost of cutting at that position. The cost will be the length of the stick from i to k plus the length of the stick from k to j, plus the minimum cost of cutting the two smaller sticks (dp[i][k] + dp[k][j]).

