<problem>
Given a binary string S, we need to find the length of the longest alternating substring. A string is called alternating if no two adjacent characters are equal.

-----Input:-----
First line contains an integer T denoting the number of test cases.
Each test case consists of a single line containing a binary string S.

-----Output:-----
For each test case print the length of the longest alternating substring in a new line.

-----Constraints-----
