The size of the cake is proportional to the time it takes to bake. So, if we know the size of the cake at a certain time, we can calculate its size at any other time.

Let's call the time when the cake is half baked $t$. Then the size of the cake at time $t$ is $2^t$. The size of the cake at time $0$ is $1$, and at time $a$ is $2^a$.

