Once we have the sizes of all the subtrees, we can find the optimal village to destroy by finding the village with the maximum subtree size. This is because destroying a village will reduce the number of fighters Naruto has to fight at once by the size of its subtree.

However, there's a catch. If we destroy a village, we can't just reduce the number of fighters by the size of its subtree. We also need to consider the number of fighters in its children. So, we need to find the village with the maximum subtree size and the minimum number of children.

