For the base case, if there are no rows left (i.e., `i == 0`), Chef earns no money. If there are no coins left in any row (i.e., `j == 0`), Chef earns no money either. For the recursive case, we need to consider two scenarios: either Chef takes a coin from the current row, or he doesn’t. If Chef takes a coin, he earns its value plus the maximum amount Chef can earn from the remaining coins in the current and subsequent rows. If he doesn’t take a coin, he earns the maximum amount Chef can earn from the remaining rows. We choose the scenario that maximizes his earnings.

