Here’s the code:

```python
def prevPermOpt1(A):
    for i in range(len(A) - 2, -1, -1):
        if A[i] > A[i + 1]:
            j = len(A) - 1
            while A[j] >= A[i]:
                j -= 1
            A[i], A[j] = A[j], A[i]
            return A
    return A
```

This solution has a time complexity of O(n^2) because we are using a nested loop. However, it is the most straightforward solution and should work for small arrays. For larger arrays, we can use a more efficient algorithm such as a binary search or a hash table to improve the time complexity....
