The solution is as follows:

```python
def twoCitySchedCost(costs):
    # Sort costs based on cost difference
    costs.sort(key=lambda x: x[0] - x[1])
    n = len(costs) // 2
    total_cost = 0
    for i in range(n):
        # Assign first half to city A and second half to city B
        total_cost += costs[i][0] + costs[i+n][1]
    return total_cost
```
