We'll start by initializing a counter for the number of iterations and the sequence. We'll then apply the median smoothing algorithm to the sequence. To do this, we'll iterate over the sequence and find the median of the current element and its neighbors. We'll then update the sequence with the median values.

We'll continue applying the median smoothing algorithm until the sequence stabilizes or until we determine that it won't stabilize. If the sequence stabilizes, we'll return the number of iterations and the resulting sequence. Otherwise, we'll return -1.

To determine if the sequence will stabilize, we'll keep track of the number of times the sequence changes between iterations. If the sequence changes more than once in a row, we'll determine that it won't stabilize and return -1.

