First, let's process the input. We'll store each person's current and desired floors, along with their position in the queue. Then we'll sort them by their desired floor, as that will help us decide the order in which we should get them into the elevator.

Next, we'll simulate the elevator's operation. We'll keep track of the elevator's current floor and the number of people it's holding. When we get to a floor with people waiting, we'll add them to the elevator if there's space and they follow the rules about entering in order.

The elevator moves up or down one floor per second, and it takes 1 second to open doors. When it opens doors, it lets out people who are at their destination and lets in people who are ready to get in.

We'll keep track of the total time taken. When all people have reached their destinations, we'll return the total time.

