<solution>
```python
def find_runner_up(scores):
    scores.sort(reverse=True)  # Sort in descending order
    runner_up = None
    for i in range(len(scores) - 1):
        if scores[i] != scores[i + 1]:
            runner_up = scores[i + 1]
            break
    return runner_up

# Test the function
scores = [2, 3, 6, 6, 5]
print(find_runner_up(scores))  # Output should be 5
```

