To find the sum of all possible edges in the graph, we can use the formula `(n * (n + 1)) / 2`. This formula calculates the sum of all numbers from 1 to n. Since we need to find the sum of all possible edges in the graph, we can multiply this sum by 2.

So, the minimum cost to visit all schools will be `(n * (n + 1)) / 2`.

<code>
```python
def min_cost_to_visit_all_schools(n):
    return (n * (n + 1)) // 2
```
