<code>
```python
def multiple_split(s, delimiters=[]):
    if not delimiters:
        return s.split()
    result = s.split(delimiters[0])
    for delimiter in delimiters[1:]:
        new_result = []
        for item in result:
            new_result.extend(item.split(delimiter))
        result = new_result
    return [item for item in result if item]
```
</code>

This solution is efficient and straightforward, handling all edge cases. It’s a clean, reliable solution that stands the test of time. Let’s test it:

