2. Flip that bit.
3. Set the bit back to its new value.

To find the value of the bit at a certain index, we can use bitwise AND (`&`) with a mask. A mask is a number with only one bit set to 1, and all other bits set to 0. For example, if we want to find the value of the bit at index 2, we can use a mask of 4 (`0b100`). This will give us the value of the bit at index 2 in the number.

To flip the bit, we can use bitwise XOR (`^`) with the mask. This will flip the bit at index 2 in the number.

To set the bit back to its new value, we can use bitwise OR (`|`) with the new value and the original number. This will set the bit at index 2 in the number to the new value.

Now, let’s put this into code:

<code>
