def flip_bit(number, index):
    mask = 1 << (index - 1)  # Create a mask with only the bit at the given index set to 1
    return (number | mask) ^ mask  # Flip the bit at the given index and set it back to its new value
```
</code>

This code works by first creating a mask with only the bit at the given index set to 1. It then flips the bit at the given index by XORing the mask with the number. Finally, it sets the bit back to its new value by ORing the result with the original number.

