Sorting is O(n log n), where n is the length of the list. Iterating through the sorted list is O(n). So, the overall time complexity is O(n log n).

Here's the code:

```python
def closest_to_zero(lst):
    lst.sort()
    closest = None
    for num in lst:
        if closest is None or abs(num) < abs(closest):
            closest = num
        elif abs(num) == abs(closest):
            return None
    return closest
```
