import re

def alphabetized(s):
    # Remove non-alphabetical characters
    s = re.sub('[^a-zA-Z]', '', s)
    # Convert to lowercase
    s = s.lower()
    # Sort and join
    return ''.join(sorted(s))

print(alphabetized("The Holy Bible"))  # Output: "BbeehHilloTy"
```

This solution is efficient and straightforward, ensuring that the output is alphabetized in case-insensitive order, with all non-alphabetical characters removed....
