3. Keep documentation up-to-date: As your code evolves over time, so should your documentation. Make sure that your comments and docstrings remain up-to-date as you make changes to your code.

4. Use consistent formatting: Consistent formatting makes it easier for others to read and understand your code.

Regarding software security, here are some tips on ensuring that your code is secure:

1. Use secure coding practices: Follow secure coding practices such as input validation, error handling, and authentication.

2. Use encryption: Use encryption whenever possible to protect sensitive data.

3. Use secure libraries: Use secure libraries that have been audited by reputable organizations.

4. Use security testing tools: Use security testing tools such as penetration testing to identify vulnerabilities in your code.

Regarding software performance monitoring, here are some tips on monitoring the performance of your applications:

