The health number is derived from the person's date of birth, which is given in YYYYMMDD format. To determine the limits, we must calculate the number of cups of coffee until any part of the health number includes "DEAD".

Since we need to handle large numbers and multiple cups of coffee, we'll use Python's built-in functions and data structures. We'll also need to convert the date of birth into the health number.

Here's a step-by-step solution:

1. Convert the date of birth into the health number.
2. Calculate the number of cups of regular coffee until any part of the health number includes "DEAD".
3. Calculate the number of cups of decaffeinated coffee until any part of the health number includes "DEAD".
4. Return an array describing the life-time coffee limits.
