For each DFS call, I’ll keep track of the current maximum number of fighters and the corresponding village. If a larger number of fighters is found, I’ll update the maximum and the corresponding village.

The DFS will start from the root node and visit all its children. For each child, the DFS will be called recursively. After visiting all children, the DFS will return to the parent node and continue with the next child.

To find the maximum number of fighters, I’ll use a variable to keep track of the maximum number of fighters found so far. If a larger number is found, I’ll update the maximum.

After the DFS is completed, I’ll return the village with the minimum number of fighters.
