Since we need to find the minimum time, we'll start by transposing the graph once and moving the token to vertex $n$. Then, we'll transpose the graph again and move the token to vertex $n$ again. We'll repeat this process until we reach vertex $n$. The time taken will be the sum of the time taken for each transposition and movement.

To implement this, we can use a queue to keep track of the vertices and the time taken to reach them. We'll start with vertex $1$ and time $0$. Then, we'll transpose the graph and move the token to vertex $n$. We'll repeat this process until we reach vertex $n$. The time taken will be the minimum time found.
