- The second line contains $N$ space-separated integers $A_i$ ($1 \leq A_i \leq 10^9$) representing the stock prices.

-----Output:-----
Print the number of ways Chef can buy exactly $K$ stocks such that the total cost is exactly $B$. Since the answer can be large, print it modulo $10^9+7$.

-----Constraints:-----
- $1 \leq T \leq 10^3$

-----Sample Input:-----
