This problem involves buying stocks such that the total cost is exactly $B$. We need to count the number of ways to buy exactly $K$ stocks such that the total cost is exactly $B$.

To solve this, we need to find all combinations of $K$ stocks whose total cost is exactly $B$. We can do this using a recursive function that tries all possible combinations of stocks.

The base case is when we have bought exactly $K$ stocks whose total cost is exactly $B$. In this case, we have found one valid combination and return 1.

